{"name":"Amber Brown","hex":"#b46a4d","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"amber","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Ambergris, the waxy product of the sperm whale. .mw-parser-output .defdate{font-size:smaller}\n\nFormerly thought to be the product of a plant.","Formerly thought to be the product of a plant."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of a brownish yellow colour, like that of most amber."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/amber"},{"term":"brown","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A colour like that of chocolate or coffee.","One of the colour balls used in snooker, with a value of 4 points."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Having a brown color/colour.","Gloomy."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/brown"}],"entries":[{"title":"Amber Brown (book series)","blocks":[{"text":"Amber Brown is a series of realistic fiction books for children created and originally written by Paula Danziger; later written by Elizabeth Levy and Bruce Coville. Early editions are illustrated by Tony Ross and later by Anthony Lewis. The original series is narrated in first person by a nine-year-old Amber Brown, starting near the end of her third grade and through the summer after her fourth grade while turning ten."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/2/21/Amber_Brown_Is_Not_a_Crayon.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Amber_Brown_(book_series)"},{"title":"Amber Brown (TV series)","blocks":[{"text":"Amber Brown is an American family comedy television series based on the book series of the same name by Paula Danziger. It premiered on July 29, 2022, on Apple TV+. In April 2023, the series was canceled after one season."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/3/33/Amber_Rose_TV_poster.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Amber_Brown_(TV_series)"},{"title":"Amber Brown (fighter)","blocks":[{"text":"Amber Brown is an American mixed martial arts (MMA) fighter in the Atomweight weight class."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Amber_Brown_(fighter)"},{"title":"Amber","blocks":[{"text":"Amber is fossilized tree resin. It has been appreciated for its color and natural beauty since Neolithic times, and worked as a gemstone since classical antiquity. Amber is used in jewelry and as a healing agent in folk medicine."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b6/Amber2.jpg/330px-Amber2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Amber"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/30/Amber_Bernstein_many_stones.jpg/500px-Amber_Bernstein_many_stones.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/30/Amber_Bernstein_many_stones.jpg/500px-Amber_Bernstein_many_stones.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Unpolished amber stones","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AAmber_Bernstein_many_stones.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/35/Amber_Fisher.jpg/500px-Amber_Fisher.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/35/Amber_Fisher.jpg/500px-Amber_Fisher.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Fishing for amber on the coast of Baltic Sea, near Gdańsk, Poland. Winter storms throw out amber nuggets.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AAmber_Fisher.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a7/Gouttes-drops-resine-2.jpg/500px-Gouttes-drops-resine-2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"h